body='''<p>Your shell stays on Oh My Zsh with Starship, fnm, pnpm, McFly, fzf and zoxide. Your familiar <code>j</code> now uses zoxide, with autojump history imported. Schnitz’s useful utilities live beside your own in <code>bin/</code>. Your aliases win when the names overlap.</p>'''
body+=table(['Command / key','Use'],[(code('pp'),'Go to ~/dev/work.'),(code('z name'),'Jump to a frequently used directory with zoxide.'),(code('j name'),'Your familiar shortcut, now an alias for zoxide’s z command.'),(code('ji name / zi name'),'Choose a directory interactively with fzf; useful when a query matches multiple projects.'),(code('ll'),'List files, including hidden files, Git status and icons with eza.'),(code('cat file'),'Read a syntax-highlighted file with bat.'),(code('rs'),'Choose and run a script from the current package.json.'),(code('ps'),'Choose a package script across this Git repository. This is your custom project command; use command ps for the system process listing.'),(code('prd / d'),'Run pnpm run dev.'),(code('prl / prt / prc'),'Run lint, type-check, or ci package scripts.'),(code('scripts'),'Show package.json scripts with jq.'),(code('lc'),'Choose a previous command from this directory. It is now placed on the prompt for review; press Return to run it.'),(keys('⌃ R'),'McFly history search, when installed.'),(keys('⌃ T')+' / '+keys('⌥ C'),'fzf file selection / directory selection. Terminal Option behavior can affect Alt-C.'),(keys('⌃ A')+' / '+keys('⌃ E'),'Beginning / end of command line.'),(keys('⌃ X')+' then '+keys('⌃ E'),'Edit the shell command in your default editor, VS Code.'),(code('find_port_blocker 3000'),'Show which process listens on a port.'),(code('kp'),'Terminate your configured backend ports: 8081, 8082, 8083, 8084 and 8086.'),(code('t file'),'Move a file to macOS Trash using the trash CLI.'),(code('mv file'),'Interactively rename one file; multi-argument mv asks before overwriting.'),(code('touchp path/to/file'),'Create missing parent directories, then the file.'),(code('mkcd parent/new-project'),'Create the directory and its parents, then enter it. Quote paths containing spaces. Stays put if creation fails.'),(code('hidedesktop / showdesktop'),'Hide or show desktop icons; Finder restarts.')])
body+='''<h3>Terminal choices</h3><p><strong>Warp is your daily terminal</strong> (<kbd>Hyper T</kbd>). It provides command/option/path completions and history-based autosuggestions, so the retired Fig hooks are unnecessary. <a href="https://docs.warp.dev/terminal/command-completions">Warp documentation</a>.</p><p><strong>Ghostty is the optional alternative</strong> when you want a native terminal with tabs and splits. Keep your usual shell commands; no need to adopt Schnitz’s tmux shortcuts. <a href="https://ghostty.org/docs/about">Ghostty documentation</a>.</p><p><strong>Herdr is worth evaluating for multiple agent sessions</strong>: its focus is persistent workspaces and status across agent terminals. It is not part of this setup. <a href="https://herdr.dev/">Herdr</a>.</p><p>In Warp, use <code>ji project</code> for an interactive directory picker: zoxide’s Space+Tab completion is not supported there. Both <code>j</code> and <code>z</code> work. <a href="https://github.com/ajeetdsouza/zoxide">Zoxide documentation</a>.</p>'''
body+='<h3>Your compact prompt</h3><p>Directory, Git branch and the usual Starship prompt symbol on the left; command duration on the right for longer commands. It uses Schnitz’s compact layout with Starship’s default colors and symbol. Edit <code>.config/starship.toml</code> in this repo; it is linked as <code>~/.starship.toml</code>. Warp must be displaying the shell prompt to show Starship.</p>'
body+='<h3>Your Git vocabulary</h3>'+table(['Command','Meaning'],[(code('git co'),'Commit. Schnitz’s checkout alias was not imported over this.'),(code('git ch branch'),'Check out a branch.'),(code('git cp'),'Interactively commit with patches.'),(code('gap'),'Stage selected hunks with git add -p.'),(code('gb / sb'),'List branches by activity / choose a branch with fzf.'),(code('gitroot / cdgr'),'Change directory to the repository root. The bin/gitroot executable prints the path.'),(code('gbb'),'Create a timestamped backup branch at the current commit.'),(code('git lg / git graph'),'Display graph views of Git history.'),(code('git pr NUMBER'),'Fetch a pull-request branch and check it out.'),(code('wip'),'Stage everything and make a Lumen-generated WIP commit, skipping hooks.'),(code('gcr'),'Your retained Lumen commit/revert/reset workflow. It changes history and skips hooks; read shell/functions.zsh before using.'),(code('git-force-pull / git-legacy'),'Retained advanced commands that can discard or rewrite work. Inspect their source before use.')])
body+='<h3>Useful additions from Schnitz</h3>'+table(['Command','Use / prerequisite'],[(code('dfile'),'Pick changed files with an fzf diff preview; needs Git, fzf, bat and delta.'),(code('dfile-list [ref]'),'Print changed file paths relative to the current directory; needs Node.'),(code('dls / dpick'),'List Docker containers / choose containers with an fzf log preview; Docker must be running.'),(code('brew-interactive'),'Choose outdated Homebrew formulae to upgrade. Escape cancels without upgrading.'),(code('pretty-json / jqi'),'JSON helpers; check the script for its expected input.'),(code('wait-until-passes "COMMAND"'),'Retry a command until it succeeds; use a command safe to repeat.'),(code('wtfeat NAME'),'Create a feature worktree under ~/dev/worktrees, using a new nirtamir/NAME branch. WORKTREE_ROOT and GIT_BRANCH_PREFIX customize the defaults.'),(code('schnizvim [file]'),'Open the optional Schnitz Neovim configuration without changing your default nvim setup.')])
