body+='<p>Fig and iTerm are retired from the managed setup. Authy, Android File Transfer, Rewind and docker-machine remain in the legacy review list. Third-party taps have not been tested by installing them.</p><p><a href="tool-inventory.json">Download the installed-tool inventory</a> · <a href="https://formulae.brew.sh/">Homebrew package catalog</a></p>'
parts.append(section('directory','06 / REFERENCE','Installed tools',body))
body='''<p>For a new Mac, copy this working checkout to a permanent folder, then run <code>./setup install</code>. Preview with <code>./setup install --dry-run</code>. Core, daily apps and the full extras list are included; <code>--minimal</code> skips extras. Existing VS Code and Warp files are preserved. The script saves a log and a checklist for account logins, keys and macOS permissions. Run <code>./setup doctor</code> to review remaining gaps. Read <code>docs/NEW-MAC.md</code> and <code>docs/MACHINE-AUDIT.md</code> for details.</p><p>The repository is the source of truth. Change a file here, then preview or apply the part you need.</p><pre><code>./setup plan                   # inspect the core links
./setup link --replace         # back up conflicts and link
./setup status                 # inspect link status
./setup packages               # report missing core packages
./setup packages core --apply  # install missing core packages
./setup shell                  # install missing shell plugins
./setup guide                  # open this local page</code></pre><p>Link backups go to <code>~/.local/state/dotfiles/backups/</code>. Each run prints an exact <code>./setup restore .../manifest.json</code> command. Restore refuses to overwrite files you changed after linking.</p>'''
body+=table(['Location','Edit here'],[(code('Brewfile / packages/'),'Core tools, extra apps, work apps, App Store apps, Node CLIs and a machine inventory.'),(code('shell/ / .zshrc'),'Your aliases, functions and shell startup.'),(code('.config/starship.toml'),'Compact prompt layout, linked as ~/.starship.toml.'),(code('bin/'),'Your executable helpers plus portable Schnitz scripts.'),(code('editors/vscode/'),'Default settings and portable Home, Work and Cursor Default profiles.'),(code('.config/schnizvim/ / .config/tmux/'),'Optional editor and terminal multiplexer configuration.'),(code('preferences/raycast-keyboard.json'),'Verified Raycast-native Hyper mapping; no Karabiner required.'),(code('raycast/'),'Your script commands and my-stuff extension source.'),(code('preferences/macos.json / preferences/desktop/'),'Active macOS and desktop restore settings. Historical YAML remains under macos-defaults/.'),(code('.private/'),'Ignored source archive and private exports; not portable through Git.'),(code('guide/'),'This offline guide and its reviewed shortcut/inventory data.')])
body+='''<h3>Raycast on a new Mac</h3><ol class="steps"><li>Install Raycast. Restore Raycast with Cloud Sync or a fresh settings export; the historical export is kept privately.</li><li>In Raycast Settings → Keyboard, set Hyper Key to Right Option and enable Include Shift.</li><li>Register this repo’s <code>raycast/scripts/quick open</code> and <code>raycast/scripts/custom</code> folders in Raycast Script Commands. Build <code>raycast/my-stuff</code> separately if you use that extension.</li><li>Set the launcher to <kbd>⌥ Space</kbd> and check every shortcut in the table against the restored settings.</li><li>Grant Accessibility permissions in macOS when the apps request them. Reconnect extension accounts inside Raycast.</li></ol><h3>What is deliberately separate</h3><p>Package installation, Mac preferences, keyboard mappings, Node tools, and optional editor setup each have their own command. Running <code>./setup</code> alone only shows help. No setup step resets Raycast, installs a different window manager, removes existing packages, or runs your old destructive installer.</p><p>Your original <code>~/dotfiles</code> remains in place. Its keyboard instructions now describe Raycast native Hyper; both repos and your live shell use zoxide-backed <code>j</code>, with Fig/iTerm startup hooks removed. Open a new Warp tab to use the updated shell. The local archive preserves authored source files; dependency folders, editor history, session databases and Git metadata were excluded. Secrets and old Raycast exports stay out of version control.</p><p>Read <code>README.md</code> and <code>docs/MIGRATION.md</code> for the complete migration decisions. To update this page after editing the reviewed data, run <code>python3 guide/build.py</code>.</p>'''
parts.append(section('manage','07 / KEEP IT YOURS','Manage this setup',body))

parts.append('<footer><a class="top-link" href="#top">Back to top ↑</a><p>Local reference. No analytics, remote assets, account data, or clipboard history.</p></footer></main></body></html>')
(G/'index.html').write_text(''.join(parts))
print('Built',G/'index.html')
